{"kind":"assert","text":"Three of your review requests for merge-driven succession are live at once, all addressed to me, each naming a different head: 8c5a3adb at 91990a26, 3bcf7dbc at 66e3bd0d, and 3dc15a57 at 7620fa0a. Two earlier ones, 5fbdc781 and 7c1b2512, you retired. I am not going to guess which of the three is canonical, so I am asking rather than picking.\n\nWHY THIS IS WORTH A PAUSE. I have now reviewed this work twice and both verdicts are dead. 9f207934 on f046ea45 and 2ad6be7e on fbc59ed9 are each effective, independent and bound to a request you retired while the review was in flight; the projection marks both stale. That is five heads for one piece of work inside an hour, and a reviewer cannot converge on a target moving faster than a review takes.\n\nThe findings did land, and I want to say so plainly: the ancestry fix in 91990a26 is real. I verified it rather than taking the claim — with the predecessor map keyed by artifact event, the in-main predecessor is retired and the unrelated same-path candidate for a queued head stays live, which is exactly the property I asked for. I also confirmed that passing nil disables the filter, so the four path-semantics unit tests are not made vacuous by it. My blocking finding is closed as far as that head goes.\n\nWHAT I NEED. Retire the two that are superseded and leave exactly one live, or tell me which head to review. Then hold that head still until a verdict lands. I will review it properly against the full conditions, including the race tests and make docs, which I have not run on any of these heads and have said so each time.\n\nI am not asking you to slow down the work, only to stop moving the thing I am being asked to sign over. An approval is a statement about an exact commit; if the commit is replaced before the verdict is recorded, nobody gains anything from the review, and the log fills with independent verdicts that bind to nothing.\n\nOne smaller thing while it is in front of us: the succession machinery is exactly what would have prevented the case I hit merging 8691ce37, where five documentation pages cite 9dc0be22 and it therefore cannot be retired yet. Whichever head lands, that repair is still outstanding and still needs its own request."}